# Workshop Library — repository & legal categories

The **Library** tab is the DM's canonical repository in the Workshop. Prep assets are stored by **category** with explicit **legal provenance**. Reference `src/lib/srd/manifest.ts`, `/legal`, and `SrdContentSource` in `src/lib/srd/types.ts`.

## Legal tiers (never violate)

| Tier | Where it lives | May ship in app? |
|------|----------------|------------------|
| **SRD (bundled)** | `src/lib/srd/` only, `source: "srd"` | Yes — CC BY 4.0, attribution required |
| **User-owned** | Browser storage only (localStorage / IndexedDB) | No — personal import or typed book content |
| **Original** | User/AI-authored lore, names, scenes | Yes as user data — not paywalled WotC rules text |

- **Never** put paywalled book rules (spells, subclasses, stat blocks) in `src/` or a shared server DB.
- **Never** merge user imports into the bundled SRD catalogue.
- Custom subclasses/spells from owned books → user tier (sheet Notes, custom fields), not `SRD_SPELLS`.

## Canonical user-facing language (use everywhere)

Use these exact terms in UI copy, help, and tutorials — source of truth is `LIBRARY_PROVENANCE_*` and `LIBRARY_ORIGIN_*` in `src/lib/workshop/libraryCatalog.ts`:

- **Included rules (SRD)** — "ships with the app — the only data we host"; read-only, never needs backup.
- **Yours (user tier)** — one tier for everything the DM owns; "this device only — never uploaded". Saved once regardless of how it arrived.
  - Origin tag **Import** — files/book content the DM brings in.
  - Origin tag **Creation** — seeds, generated results, and workshop/VTT-made parties. Creations save exactly like imports (same tier, same folder, one save) — the tag is the only difference.

Data persistence is **auto-save first and strictly one-directional**: the DM sets an **auto-save folder** once (`src/lib/workshop/librarySync.ts`, File System Access API) — a local directory or cloud-synced folder (OneDrive/Drive/Dropbox) — and every library change writes `ddeasy-library.json` there automatically (`scheduleLibrarySnapshot()` after mutations). The app **only ever writes** to that folder; it must never read data back from it automatically. Data enters the app only through the explicit **Restore backup** action (`src/lib/workshop/libraryBackup.ts`), which is also the manual fallback for unsupported browsers alongside **Export backup**. Both use the same JSON format; restores are non-destructive (merge by id, skip existing). Never invent a second export format for the same data, never make manual export the primary flow, and never auto-import from the sync folder.

## Library categories (use typed unions + labels)

Every stored item must belong to one category. Extend existing types — do not invent ad-hoc string kinds.

| Category | Type | Storage module | Typical content |
|----------|------|----------------|-----------------|
| **Seeds** | `SeedKind` | `src/lib/realmSeeds.ts` | Grounding markdown: realm, adventure, characters, maps, props |
| **Results** | `LibraryKind` | `src/lib/generationLibrary.ts` | Generated or hand-edited outputs + images |
| **Parties** | `SavedCharacterRoster` | `src/lib/tabletop/characterRoster.ts` | PC sheets, `.md` import, VTT save-back |
| **Campaigns** | `SavedCampaign` | `src/lib/campaigns.ts` | One per group the DM runs: links a party + seeds + results by id, owns a shelved VTT table |

Campaigns are containers, not copies: they hold **id references** (many-to-many for seeds/results), the active campaign scopes the Library and auto-links new creations, and opening one swaps the Virtual Table via per-campaign snapshots (`switchCampaignTable` in `src/lib/tabletop/store.ts`). Deleting a campaign never deletes linked content.

The SRD reference (`SrdCatalogue`, `src/lib/srd/`) is **not a browse category** — it is a Library *feature*: the read-only **Browse SRD rules** browser (`SrdLibraryBrowser`), toggled open over the list. Category tabs (`WorkshopLibraryCategory`) cover the DM's own content only.

New categories (monsters, items, house rules) need a new typed `kind`, a `*_LABEL` map, a storage module, a registered CI class in `src/lib/ciRegistry.ts` (see `cmdb-configuration-items` rule), and a legal review against `SRD_CONTENT_POLICY`.

## When building Library features

**Do**

- Route create / import / edit / export through the Library with a visible category badge.
- Label UI by tier where it matters: SRD picker vs "Custom (your books)" vs generated original.
- Keep SRD references as catalogue **ids** (`knownSpellIds`); keep non-SRD spells in Notes.
- Wire generators and VTT to **read from** Library seeds, results, and parties — not duplicate stores.

**Don't**

- Add a fourth parallel store for the same asset type.
- Hide provenance or blur SRD vs user-owned content.
- Default imports into bundled rules or expose user imports to other users.

## Check before shipping

1. Does this item have a **category type** and **storage module**?
2. Is provenance **SRD**, **user-owned**, or **original**?
3. Would `/legal` still be accurate after this change?

Related principles: `dm-control-tower` (manual-first) and `scale-portability` (storage modules must port to larger environments without signature changes).
